{
 "title": "Why a silo can explode",
 "style": "silo",
 "script": "The most dangerous thing on a farm might be dust.\n\nGrain dust floating in the air can explode like gunpowder.\n\nIn 1878, flour dust inside a mill in Minneapolis caught a spark. The blast flattened the building and killed eighteen workers.\n\nThat's why grain elevators have strict rules about sparks.\n\nA silo full of corn... can be a bomb.",
 "beats": [
